1
00:00:00,108 --> 00:00:04,268
From now on, "frog" is me, "sandwich"
means you, and "lemon" means rocket.

2
00:00:04,446 --> 00:00:08,546
(Howard:)So come on, sandwich, build me a lemon
because froggie wants to come home.

3
00:00:13,989 --> 00:00:15,579
(Amy:)Look at you...

4
00:00:15,824 --> 00:00:18,194
(Amy:)...putting on a brave face.

5
00:00:18,960 --> 00:00:21,450
(Penny:)There's nothing to be brave about.
Everything's fine.

6
00:00:21,630 --> 00:00:25,070
(Amy:)Really? I don't know how much
you know about primate behavior...

7
00:00:25,233 --> 00:00:28,503
(Amy:)...but Sheldon's assistant
was clearly courting Leonard.

8
00:00:28,703 --> 00:00:30,833
(Amy:)Were she a mandrill,
she would've bent over...

9
00:00:31,006 --> 00:00:35,336
...and displayed her brightly colored
hindquarters like a big red welcome mat.

10
00:00:37,145 --> 00:00:40,635
(Amy:)By the way, you try that
at the junior prom, you get kicked out.

11
00:00:42,517 --> 00:00:45,817
(Penny:)Okay, maybe she was flirting with him,
but who cares?

12
00:00:45,987 --> 00:00:48,927
(Penny:)I don't even know where
my relationship is with Leonard now.

13
00:00:49,090 --> 00:00:50,820
(Amy:)So says your prefrontal cortex.

14
00:00:50,992 --> 00:00:53,482
But the limbic system of your brain
is calculating...

15
00:00:53,662 --> 00:00:56,132
(Amy:)...that if another woman is attracted
to Leonard...

16
00:00:56,298 --> 00:00:58,128
(Amy:)...it must be because he's desirable.

17
00:00:58,300 --> 00:01:01,670
(Penny:)Well, of course he's desirable.
I mean, he's great.

